by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-02T05:24:36Z

Both blockers from the last round are gone: the property is private again, `getScheme()` became `getHttpScheme()` so it no longer collides with 8.1's private method, and the 83 constraint bumps make low-deps and high-deps green. The full sweep is fine by me, `TrackingHeader` did the same thing for 11 mailer bridges in this same release.

One thing I fixed while going through it, and pushed. `getSsl()` went through `Dsn::getBooleanOption()`, which is `filter_var($value, FILTER_VALIDATE_BOOLEAN)`, and that maps every value it does not recognise to `false`. On the patched branch:

```
ssl=''        -> http
ssl='true'    -> https
ssl='ture'    -> http
ssl='enabled' -> http
ssl='https'   -> http
no option     -> https
```

So a typo in the DSN silently dropped TLS and sent the API token in clear text. For `fast` or `test` that leniency costs nothing, for this option it is the wrong default. `getSsl()` now uses `FILTER_NULL_ON_FAILURE` and throws on anything it cannot read as a boolean. The empty value stays `false` so `?ssl=%env(bool:NOTIFIER_SSL)%` keeps working. New `AbstractTransportFactoryTest` covers both halves.

Also on my side: split the component CHANGELOG so the added `getHttpScheme()`, `SSL` and `getSsl()` are named, reworded one commit subject, and rewrote the description, which still documented `getScheme()` and `$secureHttp`. I added the points the docs PR has to carry at the end of it.

CI: Fabbot is the nine pre-existing exception-message findings in files the sweep touches, as before. The Windows job is `NativeHttpClientTest::testTimeout*`, unrelated.

One thing for later, not for this PR: `sslmode=disable` is still the spelling in `messenger/amazon-sqs` and `lock/dynamodb`. Worth unifying the same way at some point.

